## Angular structure

### Guideline

- Keep `src/main.ts` as the composition root: `bootstrapApplication`, providers, and nothing else.
- Group each feature under `src/app/<feature>/` with its components, services, guards, and routes colocated (Angular's flat layout, not a type-based tree).
- Keep `src/app/core/` for singleton services, guards, and interceptors provided once, at the root.
- Keep `src/app/shared/` for presentational components, directives, and pipes reused by several features — not a dumping ground for unrelated helpers.
- Declare the root `Routes` array in `src/app/app.routes.ts`; lazy-load features with `loadComponent`/`loadChildren`.
<!-- Project-specific / Angular-Guideline -->

### Layout

```
├── src/
│   ├── main.ts               # composition root: bootstrapApplication, providers
│   └── app/
│       ├── <feature>/        # a feature's components, services, guards, and routes, colocated
│       ├── core/             # singleton services, guards, interceptors provided once, at the root
│       ├── shared/           # presentational components, directives, pipes reused by several features
│       └── app.routes.ts     # root Routes array; features lazy-load with loadComponent/loadChildren
<!-- Project-specific / Angular-Layout -->
```

### Layer Dependencies

Notes for declaring layers in the `Layer Dependencies` section of `.attunic/context.md`; adjust them to the project before declaring.

- Components, directives, and pipes are the delivery layer: they render and adapt, they do not decide.
- Business rules are plain TypeScript classes or functions with no `@angular/*` import; declare a repository interface there and implement it in a service that injects `HttpClient`.
- Guards, interceptors, and resolvers depend on the application layer's interfaces, never the reverse.
- Prefer passing dependencies in (constructor or `inject()`) over module-level singletons, so a layer boundary can be substituted in tests.
- Check by hand: read the imports of changed files; an inner module importing an outer one is a violation.

| Layer | Typical path | Depends on | Must never contain |
|-------|--------------|------------|--------------------|
| domain | src/app/domain | itself | framework types, database, HTTP |
| application | src/app/application | domain | HTTP handlers, framework types |
| infrastructure | src/app/infrastructure, \*.service.ts, \*.interceptor.ts | application (its ports), domain | business rules |
| ui | src/app/** | application, domain | SQL, external clients |
<!-- Project-specific / Angular-Layer-Dependencies -->
